; ===============================================================
; Classification Buffer Validation Script
; ===============================================================
;
; PURPOSE: Verify the sprite classification buffer and metadata-
; backed water effect work correctly.
;
; HOW TO RUN:
;   1. Start OpenTTD and create/load a game with water visible
;   2. Open console (~)
;   3. Type: exec scripts/validate_classification.scr
;   4. Screenshots saved to OpenTTD user directory
;   5. Compare screenshots against expected behaviour
;
; EXPECTED RESULTS:
;   - vc_01_baseline: Normal rendering (reference)
;   - vc_02_debug_class: False-colour classification overlay
;     -> water=blue, trees=green, buildings=gray, vehicles=red,
;        terrain=brown, effects=yellow, unknown=dark gray
;   - vc_03_water_heuristic_off: PP on but water disabled
;   - vc_04_water_metadata: Water effect using class_tex
;     -> shimmer should appear ONLY on water tiles
;     -> no shimmer on blue roofs, vehicles, or UI
;   - vc_05_water_plus_night: Water + night mode combined
;     -> water shimmer should still work (no false positives)
;   - vc_06_restore: Should be identical to baseline
;
; ===============================================================

; === STEP 1: Baseline (PP off) ===
pp off
pp_screenshot vc_01_baseline

; === STEP 2: Classification debug view ===
pp on
pp debug_class on
pp_screenshot vc_02_debug_class

; === STEP 3: PP on, water off (baseline with PP) ===
pp debug_class off
pp disable water
pp_screenshot vc_03_water_heuristic_off

; === STEP 4: Water effect with classification metadata ===
pp enable water
pp_screenshot vc_04_water_metadata

; === STEP 5: Water + night mode (regression test for blue-tint false positives) ===
pp enable night
pp_screenshot vc_05_water_plus_night

; === STEP 6: Restore baseline ===
pp disable night
pp disable water
pp off
pp_screenshot vc_06_restore

; === STEP 7: Budget check ===
pp on
pp budget

; === Done ===
pp off
echo "Classification validation complete. Check screenshots in user directory."
